    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d661">

                <pb facs="0720" n="712" sameAs="frus:frus1939v05/pg712"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">812.6363/6337: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Mexico</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Boal</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1939-12-02T15:00:00-06:00">December 2, 1939—3
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 7:26 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>388. Second Chamber Supreme Court today unanimously upheld project of decision
                    submitted by Justice Asiain in petroleum <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >amparo</hi>.<anchor n="56" xml:id="d661-f1"/> Project of decision was
                    forwarded Department in despatch No. 9518, November 17, 1939.<anchor n="57"
                        xml:id="d661-f2"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Boal</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d661-f1" n="56" xml:id="d661-f1-content">
                <p>Cia. Mexieana de Petróleo “El Aguila,” S. A. y coags., Mexico, <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Semanario Judicial de la Federation</hi>, vol. <hi
                        rendition="#small-caps">lxii</hi>, No. 12, November 27–December 2, 1939, pp.
                    3021–3072; No. 13, December 2–6, 1939, pp. 3073–3184. Published in English in
                    Standard Oil Company of New Jersey, <hi rendition="#italic">Denials of
                        Justice</hi> (New York, 1940), pp. 49–167.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d661-f2" n="57" xml:id="d661-f2-content">
                <p>Not printed.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
